spans.s:
asita,
(1) adj. (black, and hence) inauspicious, offensive; so AMg. asiya = aśubha, Sheth, Ratnach.; not in Skt. or Pali: LV 〔327.8〕 (vs) na ca jara asitā, and (while) there is no offensive old age (so Tib. mi śis, normally = aśubha);
(2) adj. (= Pali id.; a-sita), unfettered, free: of Buddha, MPS 〔12.9〕; MSV 〔i.12.14〕;
(3) m. (= Pali id.), n. of a well-known sage, ‘the Buddhist Simeon’: LV 〔101.1 ff.〕 (his story told); 〔253.1, 15〕; Mv 〔ii.30.13 ff.〕 (his story; in 〔37.13〕 called Kāla (5), q.v., if Senart is right); 〔144.8〕; 〔151.12〕; he was the maternal uncle of Nālaka, q.v., Mv 〔iii.382.16〕; Divy 〔391.6〕;
(4) n. of a Bodhisattva: Gv 〔442.18〕;
(5) m. or nt., n. of a plant, as var. in mss. for āśītakī, q.v.
